WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.082
The module has two main halves.

00:00:02.082 --> 00:00:07.927
First, we work with text: inspect, normalize, parse, and validate.

00:00:07.927 --> 00:00:13.627
Second, we work with time: choose the correct type, extract components, change analytical grain,

00:00:13.627 --> 00:00:17.157
calculate durations, and handle time zones.

00:00:17.157 --> 00:00:20.472
At the end, we combine the ideas in practical preparation tasks and projects.

00:00:20.472 --> 00:00:28.132
Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:28.132 --> 00:00:31.242
a hospital calculating length of stay and follow-up dates.

00:00:31.242 --> 00:00:38.122
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:38.122 --> 00:00:41.677
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:41.677 --> 00:00:48.132
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to

00:00:48.132 --> 00:00:51.667
defend later: what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:55.840
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
